`sgl-router` — slim KV-aware OpenAI-compatible router for SGLang workers.

Discovery is mutually exclusive: pass `--worker-urls` for a static worker list, or `--service-discovery` for Kubernetes EndpointSlice discovery — exactly one is required.

Usage: sgl-router [OPTIONS] --model-id <MODEL_ID>

Options:
      --host <HOST>
          Address to bind the HTTP server to
          
          [default: 127.0.0.1]

      --port <PORT>
          Port to bind the HTTP server to
          
          [default: 30000]

      --admin-api-key <ADMIN_API_KEY>
          Require `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on router admin endpoints. When omitted, admin endpoints remain unauthenticated for compatibility

      --model-id <MODEL_ID>
          Model id this router serves (the OpenAI `model` field)

      --tokenizer-path <TOKENIZER_PATH>
          Tokenizer source: a local `tokenizer.json` path, or a HuggingFace repo id to download from. When omitted, falls back to `--model-id` as the repo id (download honors `HF_TOKEN` / `HF_HOME`)

      --policy <POLICY>
          Routing policy

          Possible values:
          - round_robin
          - random
          - power_of_two
          - load_based:    Selects the currently least-loaded worker
          - fused_score:   Weighted sum of `--fuse` terms
          - score_policy:  Composes compatible scoring terms into a single routing policy
          - session_aware: Selects a worker from session affinity
          - cache_aware:   Selects cache-affine prefill candidates from the configured prefix provider
          - sticky:        Sticky-session routing: pins a routing key (read from a configurable request header) to a worker via an in-memory map, so stateful sessions land on the same backend. Tuning — header name, keyless-fallback policy, and TTL eviction — lives on `ModelConfig::sticky`
          
          [default: round_robin]

      --decode-policy <DECODE_POLICY>
          Policy used to select decode workers for PD requests
          
          [default: power_of_two]
          [possible values: power_of_two, legacy_host_affinity]

      --bucket-config <BUCKET_CONFIG>
          Static P/D bucket configuration. Omit to use the global candidate domain

      --cb-threshold <CB_THRESHOLD>
          Consecutive upstream failures before the circuit breaker opens. Setting this enables the circuit breaker; `0` is rejected

      --cb-cool-down-secs <CB_COOL_DOWN_SECS>
          Circuit-breaker cool-down in seconds. Only meaningful with `--cb-threshold`; defaults to 30 when the breaker is enabled

      --kv-indexer-endpoint <KV_INDEXER_ENDPOINT>
          External KV indexer gRPC endpoint used as the authoritative cache signal. Needs an explicit scheme, e.g. `http://10.0.0.1:50051`

      --kv-indexer-query-timeout-ms <KV_INDEXER_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS>
          KV Indexer query timeout in milliseconds. Requires `--kv-indexer-endpoint`; defaults to 100

      --kv-indexer-query-max-inflight <KV_INDEXER_QUERY_MAX_INFLIGHT>
          Maximum concurrent KV Indexer queries issued by this Router. Requires `--kv-indexer-endpoint`; defaults to 32

      --cache-prefix-provider <CACHE_PREFIX_PROVIDER>
          Prefix-match source for native Cache-Aware
          
          [possible values: radix_tree, indexer]

      --session-id-header <SESSION_ID_HEADER>
          Header carrying the session ID for `--policy session_aware`

      --session-idle-secs <SESSION_IDLE_SECS>
          Idle timeout for a session assignment, in seconds

      --session-eviction-interval-secs <SESSION_EVICTION_INTERVAL_SECS>
          Session-assignment eviction cadence, in seconds

      --stable-pair
          Use a deterministic backup for the affinity key and candidate range

      --affinity-mode <AFFINITY_MODE>
          Session-affinity admission mode

          Possible values:
          - strict: Keep the primary after it passes admission
          - soft:   Allow the admitted backup to relieve pressure

      --session-affinity-mode <SESSION_AFFINITY_MODE>
          Session-affinity primary lookup and fallback behavior

          Possible values:
          - bucket:          Search only within the target bucket
          - global-rebind:   Rebind to a target-bucket fallback when the global primary is unavailable
          - global-preserve: Keep a valid global assignment when a bucket fallback is used

      --disable-pressure-guard
          Disables the Session/Cache-Aware pressure guard

      --pressure-abs-threshold-tokens <PRESSURE_ABS_THRESHOLD_TOKENS>
          Absolute waiting-uncached-token gap required by the pressure guard

      --pressure-abs-threshold-ms <PRESSURE_ABS_THRESHOLD_MS>
          Absolute millisecond gap when a Prefill queue estimate is available

      --pressure-rel-threshold <PRESSURE_REL_THRESHOLD>
          Relative waiting-uncached-token multiplier required by the pressure guard

      --cache-affinity-min-matched-tokens <CACHE_AFFINITY_MIN_MATCHED_TOKENS>
          Minimum cache-hit tokens for a cache-aware candidate

      --cache-affinity-min-match-ratio <CACHE_AFFINITY_MIN_MATCH_RATIO>
          Minimum cache-hit ratio for a cache-aware candidate

      --cache-candidate-min-workers <CACHE_CANDIDATE_MIN_WORKERS>
          Minimum number of cache-aware candidates to try

      --cache-candidate-ratio <CACHE_CANDIDATE_RATIO>
          Fraction of healthy prefill workers considered as cache-aware candidates

      --cache-candidate-max-workers <CACHE_CANDIDATE_MAX_WORKERS>
          Maximum number of cache-aware candidates to try

      --cache-switch-margin-tokens <CACHE_SWITCH_MARGIN_TOKENS>
          Maximum uncached-work difference that pressure may override

      --fuse <FUSE>
          Policies to sum, spelled exactly as `--policy` spells them and each optionally weighted: `--fuse prefix_cache=2.0,load_based=0.3`. An omitted weight keeps that policy's own default. Requires `--policy score_policy` or `fused_score`; when either policy is set and this flag is omitted, the terms default to `prefix_cache,load_based`

      --filter <FILTER>
          Ordered hard constraints applied before policy selection

          Possible values:
          - overloaded:   Router-local in-flight capacity limit
          - prefix_cache: Requires a minimum share of cached prompt blocks

      --max-in-flight <MAX_IN_FLIGHT>
          Router-local in-flight limit for `--filter overloaded`

      --prefix-cache-min-share <PREFIX_CACHE_MIN_SHARE>
          Minimum cached prompt share for `--filter prefix_cache`

      --routing-key-header <ROUTING_KEY_HEADER>
          Request header carrying the routing key for sticky-session routing. Defaults to `x-sgl-routing-key` when `--policy sticky` is set

      --sticky-fallback-policy <STICKY_FALLBACK_POLICY>
          Policy used to select a worker for requests with no routing key, and to pick the initial worker when a new key is first seen. One of `round_robin` / `random` / `power_of_two` / `load_based`. Defaults to `round_robin`
          
          [possible values: round_robin, random, power_of_two, load_based]

      --sticky-idle-secs <STICKY_IDLE_SECS>
          Evict a sticky assignment after it has been idle (unreferenced) this many seconds. Defaults to 600

      --sticky-eviction-interval-secs <STICKY_EVICTION_INTERVAL_SECS>
          Wall-clock cadence of the sticky idle-eviction sweep, in seconds. Defaults to 60

      --worker-urls <WORKER_URLS>...
          Static worker URLs (space-separated or repeated). Mutually exclusive with `--service-discovery`

      --service-discovery
          Enable Kubernetes EndpointSlice discovery

      --service-discovery-namespace <SERVICE_DISCOVERY_NAMESPACE>
          Namespace to watch. Unset/empty watches all namespaces (requires cluster-wide RBAC)

      --selector <SELECTOR>...
          Plain-mode label selector terms, e.g. `app=engines-qwen3` (space-separated or repeated `key=value`, AND-joined). Mutually exclusive with the prefill/decode selectors

      --prefill-selector <PREFILL_SELECTOR>...
          PD-mode prefill label selector terms. Requires `--decode-selector`

      --decode-selector <DECODE_SELECTOR>...
          PD-mode decode label selector terms. Requires `--prefill-selector`

      --request-timeout-secs <REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS>
          Per-request upstream timeout in seconds
          
          [default: 300]

      --stale-request-timeout-secs <STALE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS>
          Max lifetime of an in-flight request entry before the janitor reaps it (returns 504 `stale_request_expired`)
          
          [default: 600]

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Default tracing level (overridden by `RUST_LOG`)
          
          [default: info]

      --log-format <LOG_FORMAT>
          Log output format
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
